---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SubscribeForm from '../../components/SubscribeForm.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Free Printable Prenup Checklist (17 Points) | PrenupAnswers"
  description="The 17-point prenup checklist as a printable PDF — disclosure, terms, and execution in order, plus the never-include list. Free download."
  noindex={true}
>
  <section class="article-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/free/">Free Downloads</a> / Checklist</p>
      <h1>The 17-Point Prenup Checklist</h1>
      <p class="meta">Printable PDF · 2 pages · free forever</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container read">
      <div class="tldr">
        <b>What you get</b>
        <p>
          One worksheet, two printed pages. Every item a valid prenup must cover — worked in the order that
          actually matters: <strong>disclosure → terms → execution</strong>. Tick the boxes together; anything
          you can't tick becomes this week's conversation, not next month's.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Layer 1 — Disclosure:</strong> assets, debts, income, inheritances, and the exhibit rule that kills prenups when skipped.</li>
        <li><strong>Layer 2 — Terms:</strong> the house, the business, support, retirement, life insurance, inheritance rights — plus the ring-fence for blended families.</li>
        <li><strong>Layer 3 — Execution:</strong> timing, voluntariness, counsel, and your state's signing formalities.</li>
        <li><strong>The never-include list:</strong> the five clauses that only create holes opponents can attack.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="isca-cta">
        <p class="eyebrow">Free download</p>
        <h4>Enter your email — the PDF lands on the next screen</h4>
        <p>Also get The Prenup Brief, our one-a-week email. Unsubscribe anytime.</p>
        <SubscribeForm variant="block" cta="Send me the checklist" source="lead-checklist" />
      </div>

      <p>
        <strong>Prefer screen to paper?</strong> The full guide behind this worksheet — with the "why"
        behind every box — is <a href="/guides/prenup-checklist/">The Prenup Checklist: 17 Things to Include</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
